WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.083 --> 00:00:04.374
- Hello Believe Nation.

00:00:04.374 --> 00:00:06.461
Today I'm going to talk
about the seven ways

00:00:06.461 --> 00:00:09.602
to structure your day for success.

00:00:09.602 --> 00:00:12.524
- [Computerized Voice] Nine, eight.

00:00:12.524 --> 00:00:15.191
(hip hop music)

00:00:17.293 --> 00:00:18.999
- So one of the most common
questions that I get asked,

00:00:18.999 --> 00:00:20.640
is how do I structure my day?

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.038
How do I set up my schedule,
my time, to have success?

00:00:24.038 --> 00:00:24.871
Consistently.

00:00:24.871 --> 00:00:25.769
Be productive.

00:00:25.769 --> 00:00:27.012
Because as an entrepreneur,

00:00:27.012 --> 00:00:28.931
you've got a million things going on.

00:00:28.931 --> 00:00:30.695
You're wearing every hat in the business.

00:00:30.695 --> 00:00:31.528
And, oh by the way,

00:00:31.528 --> 00:00:33.210
you want a personal life, as well.

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:34.901
So today I'm going to share with you

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:39.068
the seven ways to structure
your day for optimal success.

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:44.815
Way number one is you need
to have a morning routine.

00:00:44.815 --> 00:00:47.167
You need to have a morning
routine that inspires you,

00:00:47.167 --> 00:00:49.060
that gets you set up from the beginning,

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:51.146
from the start of every single day

00:00:51.146 --> 00:00:52.652
to set you up for success.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:54.481
This is one of the biggest things

00:00:54.481 --> 00:00:55.796
that entrepreneurs need help with

00:00:55.796 --> 00:00:57.540
because, maybe you watch this video,

00:00:57.540 --> 00:00:59.027
on a Thursday afternoon at five o'clock,

00:00:59.027 --> 00:01:00.371
and you're working so hard,

00:01:00.371 --> 00:01:01.721
you get so inspired and motivated,

00:01:01.721 --> 00:01:03.115
or maybe you're meeting somebody.

00:01:03.115 --> 00:01:05.822
Or maybe you listen to
a podcast or something.

00:01:05.822 --> 00:01:07.669
Think about what gets you so inspired

00:01:07.669 --> 00:01:08.783
because, often what happens,

00:01:08.783 --> 00:01:10.755
is then you have tons of productivity,

00:01:10.755 --> 00:01:13.042
and then you wake up the
next day and it's gonea

00:01:13.042 --> 00:01:13.885
and you're starting over

00:01:13.885 --> 00:01:16.325
and the alarm goes off
and you're sluggish,

00:01:16.325 --> 00:01:18.374
getting out of bed and
you don't want to do it.

00:01:18.374 --> 00:01:21.184
And you slowly grind into your day.

00:01:21.184 --> 00:01:22.993
Until some other random thing happens,

00:01:22.993 --> 00:01:25.591
and that gets you fired up
and you're off and running.

00:01:25.591 --> 00:01:27.329
And instead of having
these peaks and valleys,

00:01:27.329 --> 00:01:28.688
where you're up and down and up and down,

00:01:28.688 --> 00:01:30.275
you're riding this roller coaster,

00:01:30.275 --> 00:01:33.407
you want to think about
what gets you most excited,

00:01:33.407 --> 00:01:35.224
motivated, inspired, productive,

00:01:35.224 --> 00:01:38.870
and plan that into your
morning routine daily.

00:01:38.870 --> 00:01:40.686
To give yourself the best shot,

00:01:40.686 --> 00:01:42.196
at having a productive day today,

00:01:42.196 --> 00:01:44.043
where you're going to go
off and have a big impact.

00:01:44.043 --> 00:01:45.941
Where you believe in the big,

00:01:45.941 --> 00:01:47.670
crazy dream that you have,

00:01:47.670 --> 00:01:49.983
that you can make it happen.

00:01:49.983 --> 00:01:51.398
Put that into your morning routine.

00:01:51.398 --> 00:01:53.121
And so for everybody it's
a little bit different.

00:01:53.121 --> 00:01:54.228
Some of the common themes,

00:01:54.228 --> 00:01:55.450
it could be having music.

00:01:55.450 --> 00:01:57.591
I love putting music on
first thing in the morning.

00:01:57.591 --> 00:01:59.179
Something that gets me
inspired and pumped up,

00:01:59.179 --> 00:02:00.871
and moving, and dancing.

00:02:00.871 --> 00:02:02.217
I love watching videos.

00:02:02.217 --> 00:02:03.050
The top 10's.

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:04.352
The mentor me's.

00:02:04.352 --> 00:02:06.362
I love reading books.

00:02:06.362 --> 00:02:08.820
I love having a exercise routine.

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:09.997
Things that get me going.

00:02:09.997 --> 00:02:11.052
This is what works for me.

00:02:11.052 --> 00:02:12.589
You need to find what works for you

00:02:12.589 --> 00:02:13.663
and the best way to do it

00:02:13.663 --> 00:02:16.808
is think about when you
have already been inspired.

00:02:16.808 --> 00:02:18.371
Because you have.

00:02:18.371 --> 00:02:19.995
'Cause you may not wake
up every day inspired,

00:02:19.995 --> 00:02:22.812
but you have been inspired
in your life before.

00:02:22.812 --> 00:02:24.621
Chances are it's happened recently to you.

00:02:24.621 --> 00:02:27.495
What happened that led
to that inspiration?

00:02:27.495 --> 00:02:29.385
And, again, instead of letting that thing

00:02:29.385 --> 00:02:30.897
be this random occurrence

00:02:30.897 --> 00:02:34.137
plan for it daily into
your morning routine

00:02:34.137 --> 00:02:37.470
to set yourself up for a successful day.

00:02:39.709 --> 00:02:42.295
Number two is ask yourself the question.

00:02:42.295 --> 00:02:45.097
The most important question
that you can ask yourself

00:02:45.097 --> 00:02:48.245
every single day is what is the most value

00:02:48.245 --> 00:02:50.611
I can bring to my business today?

00:02:50.611 --> 00:02:52.346
This is something I'm obsessed with.

00:02:52.346 --> 00:02:54.618
And every day as I'm
walking to the office,

00:02:54.618 --> 00:02:56.926
or walking here to Toronto Dance Salsa,

00:02:56.926 --> 00:02:59.431
I'm thinking about what's
the most value that I can

00:02:59.431 --> 00:03:01.229
bring to my business today.

00:03:01.229 --> 00:03:04.065
Because you have a ton
of things on your plate.

00:03:04.065 --> 00:03:04.898
Right?

00:03:04.898 --> 00:03:05.830
Entrepreneurs that I know,

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.604
have a to do list this long,

00:03:07.604 --> 00:03:10.588
followed by an ideas list
which is even longer.

00:03:10.588 --> 00:03:11.421
Right?

00:03:11.421 --> 00:03:12.278
Sound familiar?

00:03:12.278 --> 00:03:13.938
You need to focus on the thing

00:03:13.938 --> 00:03:16.135
that's going to bring the most immediate,

00:03:16.135 --> 00:03:18.762
impactful value to your business.

00:03:18.762 --> 00:03:20.960
Especially if you're a solo entrepreneur.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:22.140
Especially if you don't have a team

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:24.444
to take care of some
of the things for you.

00:03:24.444 --> 00:03:27.193
When you are literally doing
everything in your business

00:03:27.193 --> 00:03:31.722
ask yourself every day what
is the highest value task

00:03:31.722 --> 00:03:35.113
that I can do today that
will advance my goals.

00:03:35.113 --> 00:03:37.113
And then go and do that.

00:03:40.019 --> 00:03:42.404
Number three is have CEO time.

00:03:42.404 --> 00:03:44.271
This ties into the last point.

00:03:44.271 --> 00:03:46.376
You need to make sure
that every single day,

00:03:46.376 --> 00:03:47.962
when you're going to your business,

00:03:47.962 --> 00:03:49.638
whether that is actually
going to an office,

00:03:49.638 --> 00:03:51.744
if you're sitting down in
front of your computer at home,

00:03:51.744 --> 00:03:53.508
or going to a Starbucks,

00:03:53.508 --> 00:03:55.701
that you have CEO time every day.

00:03:55.701 --> 00:03:58.425
And CEO time, what I
consider to be CEO time,

00:03:58.425 --> 00:04:02.928
is time to focus on the business
instead of in the business.

00:04:02.928 --> 00:04:04.593
Or yes, you have a million things to do.

00:04:04.593 --> 00:04:06.004
You've got tons of emails to get back to.

00:04:06.004 --> 00:04:08.380
You've got lots of social
media to post out there.

00:04:08.380 --> 00:04:10.089
Everybody wants a piece of you.

00:04:10.089 --> 00:04:12.944
And you've got an ideas list,
again, that's a mile long.

00:04:12.944 --> 00:04:14.520
You need to have CEO time.

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.911
I recommend at least 90
minutes a day of CEO time.

00:04:17.911 --> 00:04:19.494
Where you're not just caught,

00:04:19.494 --> 00:04:21.039
in the day-to-day running of the business,

00:04:21.039 --> 00:04:22.817
and stuck on that mouse wheel.

00:04:22.817 --> 00:04:23.719
You're just going around
and around and around

00:04:23.719 --> 00:04:25.153
and around in circles.

00:04:25.153 --> 00:04:28.668
If you don't ever have
time to focus on planning,

00:04:28.668 --> 00:04:30.351
and the bigger picture of your business,

00:04:30.351 --> 00:04:31.242
then guess what?

00:04:31.242 --> 00:04:32.990
You're never going to
get to the bigger picture

00:04:32.990 --> 00:04:33.823
for your business.

00:04:33.823 --> 00:04:36.166
You're going to stay stuck where you are.

00:04:36.166 --> 00:04:39.071
So plan CEO time every
day into your business.

00:04:39.071 --> 00:04:41.050
I prefer it in the morning.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:43.114
I prefer it before you open up your email,

00:04:43.114 --> 00:04:44.691
before you let your day explode on you.

00:04:44.691 --> 00:04:46.036
'Cause you wake up.

00:04:46.036 --> 00:04:47.126
You go to the office.

00:04:47.126 --> 00:04:48.324
You look at your email.

00:04:48.324 --> 00:04:49.734
And suddenly, your day is over.

00:04:49.734 --> 00:04:52.335
You're just constantly
responding to other people.

00:04:52.335 --> 00:04:53.979
So whether you call it eat that frog,

00:04:53.979 --> 00:04:55.569
or first priorities first,

00:04:55.569 --> 00:04:57.759
or lots of people have
different names for it.

00:04:57.759 --> 00:05:00.043
Making sure that you plan
that into your schedule

00:05:00.043 --> 00:05:02.889
before your day blows
up on you is important

00:05:02.889 --> 00:05:04.908
if you want to escape where you are.

00:05:04.908 --> 00:05:07.321
Because otherwise, you're
going to stay here.

00:05:07.321 --> 00:05:10.571
Instead of being able to grow out here.

00:05:12.312 --> 00:05:14.412
Number four is chunk your time.

00:05:14.412 --> 00:05:16.791
Anything that you do
multiple times per day,

00:05:16.791 --> 00:05:20.023
you want to try to chunk it
down to one time per day.

00:05:20.023 --> 00:05:23.843
It makes a huge, huge, huge
difference in your productivity,

00:05:23.843 --> 00:05:25.131
in how you structure it,

00:05:25.131 --> 00:05:27.805
so that you can get more
important stuff done.

00:05:27.805 --> 00:05:30.936
And the classic one is
emails or phone calls.

00:05:30.936 --> 00:05:33.687
Because, if somebody emails
you and you look at it,

00:05:33.687 --> 00:05:35.952
even if you don't address it immediately,

00:05:35.952 --> 00:05:38.023
it's still, you're thinking about it.

00:05:38.023 --> 00:05:41.100
And it distracted you from
doing what you should be doing.

00:05:41.100 --> 00:05:43.110
Which is whatever task you're working on.

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.423
And this is especially important

00:05:44.423 --> 00:05:46.353
when you're doing creative tasks.

00:05:46.353 --> 00:05:47.595
When I'm working on my book,

00:05:47.595 --> 00:05:49.068
when I'm writing the manuscript,

00:05:49.068 --> 00:05:50.831
when I'm doing important research.

00:05:50.831 --> 00:05:53.078
I'm so in the zone of focus there

00:05:53.078 --> 00:05:55.327
that if you tap me on the shoulder,

00:05:55.327 --> 00:05:56.308
or you send me an email,

00:05:56.308 --> 00:05:57.672
or you try to call me,

00:05:57.672 --> 00:05:58.641
I don't have a phone but,

00:05:58.641 --> 00:05:59.824
you try to call me,

00:05:59.824 --> 00:06:03.461
it takes me half an hour just
to get back to where I was.

00:06:03.461 --> 00:06:06.060
So that five second
interruption isn't really

00:06:06.060 --> 00:06:07.288
a five second interruption.

00:06:07.288 --> 00:06:09.449
You've screwed over a
good chunk of my day.

00:06:09.449 --> 00:06:12.493
And so thinking about those
important things that happened

00:06:12.493 --> 00:06:14.343
to you multiple times per day,

00:06:14.343 --> 00:06:15.767
how do you chunk that down

00:06:15.767 --> 00:06:17.653
so I'm only doing it one time a day,

00:06:17.653 --> 00:06:19.749
I'm focused on just
doing that for the day,

00:06:19.749 --> 00:06:21.542
and it means that you lose,

00:06:21.542 --> 00:06:23.681
you lose some small potential wins.

00:06:23.681 --> 00:06:24.514
Right?

00:06:24.514 --> 00:06:26.758
Like if you're only
checking email at 12 o'clock

00:06:26.758 --> 00:06:28.272
as an example,

00:06:28.272 --> 00:06:31.818
then maybe some really important
media opportunity comes up

00:06:31.818 --> 00:06:33.630
and they need an answer by 11 o'clock.

00:06:33.630 --> 00:06:35.680
And you didn't see it in time and so,

00:06:35.680 --> 00:06:37.532
you don't get that media opportunity.

00:06:37.532 --> 00:06:40.103
You can't get every single small win.

00:06:40.103 --> 00:06:40.959
It's not going to happen.

00:06:40.959 --> 00:06:41.792
It's not possible.

00:06:41.792 --> 00:06:43.219
You can't be on 24/7.

00:06:43.219 --> 00:06:44.512
It is not possible.

00:06:44.512 --> 00:06:45.712
And so you have to be comfortable

00:06:45.712 --> 00:06:47.355
with losing some of the small wins

00:06:47.355 --> 00:06:50.850
because the time that your
spending that is so focused

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:53.690
is allowing you to go create
something bigger and amazing.

00:06:53.690 --> 00:06:55.523
Chunk your daily time.

00:06:58.164 --> 00:07:00.061
Number five is chunk your week.

00:07:00.061 --> 00:07:03.288
So just like we chunk multiple
times per day to once a day,

00:07:03.288 --> 00:07:05.401
anything you're doing
multiple times per week,

00:07:05.401 --> 00:07:07.072
do once per week.

00:07:07.072 --> 00:07:09.691
So I look at the filming
videos as an example.

00:07:09.691 --> 00:07:12.024
I film all the videos for my channel

00:07:12.024 --> 00:07:13.463
pretty much on a Wednesday afternoon.

00:07:13.463 --> 00:07:15.435
I'll stand here at Toronto Dance Salsa,

00:07:15.435 --> 00:07:17.561
I'll set up the lights and
the gear and the camera

00:07:17.561 --> 00:07:20.556
and the books and the
microphone and all that,

00:07:20.556 --> 00:07:22.734
and make 20 videos for the week.

00:07:22.734 --> 00:07:24.042
And it does a couple of things.

00:07:24.042 --> 00:07:25.381
Why is this so important?

00:07:25.381 --> 00:07:28.077
Like why not do three videos a day?

00:07:28.077 --> 00:07:31.171
Instead of 20 videos in one day.

00:07:31.171 --> 00:07:33.869
One, because there's setup
time and take down time.

00:07:33.869 --> 00:07:35.341
This applies to anything.

00:07:35.341 --> 00:07:36.256
Whatever you want to get into,

00:07:36.256 --> 00:07:37.387
whatever tasks you have,

00:07:37.387 --> 00:07:39.634
there's set up time and take down time.

00:07:39.634 --> 00:07:40.509
For this,

00:07:40.509 --> 00:07:42.409
I need to set up the lights
and the camera and the books,

00:07:42.409 --> 00:07:43.695
and the microphone and all that stuff.

00:07:43.695 --> 00:07:45.241
I need to get it all ready.

00:07:45.241 --> 00:07:47.775
And so it's much more time saving

00:07:47.775 --> 00:07:50.943
for me to do it all at once,
all the videos at once,

00:07:50.943 --> 00:07:51.776
instead of having that setup

00:07:51.776 --> 00:07:53.759
and take down time each time.

00:07:53.759 --> 00:07:57.665
The second thing is task
switching is difficult.

00:07:57.665 --> 00:08:00.118
So when I'm in video
mode, I'm in video mode.

00:08:00.118 --> 00:08:01.631
I'm just focused on the videos.

00:08:01.631 --> 00:08:03.706
I can bring the energy from
one video to the next video

00:08:03.706 --> 00:08:05.685
to the next video, where
it's so hard for me

00:08:05.685 --> 00:08:08.869
to go from video mode,
extrovertive, energy,

00:08:08.869 --> 00:08:12.702
enthusiasm, into research mode

00:08:12.702 --> 00:08:14.858
where it's headphones on,

00:08:14.858 --> 00:08:18.047
don't talk to me, introverted, analyzing,

00:08:18.047 --> 00:08:19.762
try to figure stuff out.

00:08:19.762 --> 00:08:21.365
And to take me from that state,

00:08:21.365 --> 00:08:23.096
introverted, getting work done,

00:08:23.096 --> 00:08:25.133
to hey come and be on a video,

00:08:25.133 --> 00:08:27.649
I'm going to have energy like this.

00:08:27.649 --> 00:08:29.535
I'm going to be distracted.

00:08:29.535 --> 00:08:32.096
I'm not going to be as upbeat.

00:08:32.096 --> 00:08:34.478
I'm going to be thinking
about other things

00:08:34.478 --> 00:08:36.634
and it won't be a good video.

00:08:36.634 --> 00:08:39.477
Even now, I already have less energy.

00:08:39.477 --> 00:08:41.655
Who wants this on video?

00:08:41.655 --> 00:08:46.393
And so, understanding that
your energy will change

00:08:46.393 --> 00:08:49.231
with different kinds
of tasks is important.

00:08:49.231 --> 00:08:51.508
And so whatever is happening
multiple times per week,

00:08:51.508 --> 00:08:54.239
try to do it on one day per week.

00:08:54.239 --> 00:08:56.319
So for me, what my
schedule looks like now,

00:08:56.319 --> 00:08:59.150
Monday I'm working on
all the video research,

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:00.235
for this channel.

00:09:00.235 --> 00:09:02.340
Reviewing all the videos,
seeing what has to be changed,

00:09:02.340 --> 00:09:03.657
what I like, what I don't like.

00:09:03.657 --> 00:09:04.724
Making modifications.

00:09:04.724 --> 00:09:07.801
And in the afternoon, I'm
doing book promotion work.

00:09:07.801 --> 00:09:09.341
Could be research again on the book

00:09:09.341 --> 00:09:10.940
or it could be reaching out to influencers

00:09:10.940 --> 00:09:13.075
or could be making thank-you videos.

00:09:13.075 --> 00:09:14.586
I'm kind of in that zone.

00:09:14.586 --> 00:09:16.614
Tuesdays, I spend the
whole afternoon doing

00:09:16.614 --> 00:09:17.990
Toronto Dance Salsa work.

00:09:17.990 --> 00:09:20.429
Wednesdays, I'm doing
videos all afternoon.

00:09:20.429 --> 00:09:21.989
Thursdays, I'm doing phone calls

00:09:21.989 --> 00:09:23.492
and interviews and meetings.

00:09:23.492 --> 00:09:25.453
And, then Friday, is my CEO day.

00:09:25.453 --> 00:09:26.420
When I'm spending the whole day doing

00:09:26.420 --> 00:09:28.023
CEO bigger picture stuff.

00:09:28.023 --> 00:09:30.022
And it really, really,
really, really, really,

00:09:30.022 --> 00:09:31.619
really, works and, again,

00:09:31.619 --> 00:09:33.880
you have to be willing
to give up the small

00:09:33.880 --> 00:09:36.213
wins to go for the big wins.

00:09:39.261 --> 00:09:41.381
Number six is value your time.

00:09:41.381 --> 00:09:43.282
I don't think people
value their time enough.

00:09:43.282 --> 00:09:44.858
I don't think entrepreneurs
value their time enough.

00:09:44.858 --> 00:09:46.423
If I audited your day and
looked at what you were

00:09:46.423 --> 00:09:50.248
actually doing the day, there'd
be a lot of wasted time.

00:09:50.248 --> 00:09:52.903
All the time you spend
on Facebook, or clicking

00:09:52.903 --> 00:09:56.323
refresh on your statistics,
to see how many people watch

00:09:56.323 --> 00:09:58.332
your YouTube videos in the past hour

00:09:58.332 --> 00:10:00.182
and going back and checking again.

00:10:00.182 --> 00:10:01.328
Or checking your sales numbers

00:10:01.328 --> 00:10:03.514
over and over and over and over again.

00:10:03.514 --> 00:10:05.766
Yes you could work harder.

00:10:05.766 --> 00:10:08.860
Yes you can add more hours to your day.

00:10:08.860 --> 00:10:11.251
Because you need to get more work done.

00:10:11.251 --> 00:10:14.375
But I would say that a huge
chunk of your current day,

00:10:14.375 --> 00:10:16.882
even if you worked zero extra hours,

00:10:16.882 --> 00:10:18.572
could be way more productive

00:10:18.572 --> 00:10:20.506
because you're just not focused.

00:10:20.506 --> 00:10:22.383
And that's a harsh truth.

00:10:22.383 --> 00:10:25.756
That's something that's hard
to say and hard to realize.

00:10:25.756 --> 00:10:27.554
But if you look at your schedule,

00:10:27.554 --> 00:10:30.160
you look at the tasks you're
actually doing during the day,

00:10:30.160 --> 00:10:32.634
and you constantly self-audit to say,

00:10:32.634 --> 00:10:36.387
is this really the best use of my time?

00:10:36.387 --> 00:10:39.045
And then start to make
adjustments based off of that.

00:10:39.045 --> 00:10:40.712
Because a lot of entrepreneurs
complain that they don't

00:10:40.712 --> 00:10:42.848
have enough time, but really,

00:10:42.848 --> 00:10:45.168
you're not valuing your time enough.

00:10:45.168 --> 00:10:49.335
And you're doing things
that you shouldn't be doing.

00:10:50.404 --> 00:10:53.457
And number seven is to invest in yourself.

00:10:53.457 --> 00:10:54.831
I'd make sure that you find time

00:10:54.831 --> 00:10:57.711
at least once a week, if not every day,

00:10:57.711 --> 00:10:59.275
to invest in yourself.

00:10:59.275 --> 00:11:00.144
To learn.

00:11:00.144 --> 00:11:01.089
To grow.

00:11:01.089 --> 00:11:02.137
To try new things.

00:11:02.137 --> 00:11:03.441
To make yourself better.

00:11:03.441 --> 00:11:04.718
Because as you grow,

00:11:04.718 --> 00:11:06.915
as you gain in knowledge and experience,

00:11:06.915 --> 00:11:09.447
and expertise, your business will grow.

00:11:09.447 --> 00:11:10.596
And so that could be,

00:11:10.596 --> 00:11:12.729
meditation, works really
well for some people.

00:11:12.729 --> 00:11:13.803
It could be gratitude.

00:11:13.803 --> 00:11:15.962
I have a daily gratitude
practice that I do

00:11:15.962 --> 00:11:17.821
every single day to remind
me of the things that I have

00:11:17.821 --> 00:11:19.307
and I'm fortunate in my life.

00:11:19.307 --> 00:11:22.307
It could be watching videos
to learn and be inspired.

00:11:22.307 --> 00:11:23.707
It could be reading.

00:11:23.707 --> 00:11:26.010
It could be trying to
understand a new topic.

00:11:26.010 --> 00:11:27.484
It fills you.

00:11:27.484 --> 00:11:28.934
It makes you feel better.

00:11:28.934 --> 00:11:30.440
It puts you in a better mood.

00:11:30.440 --> 00:11:33.836
And it gives you more
of not just inspiration

00:11:33.836 --> 00:11:36.008
but also the tactics of what to do.

00:11:36.008 --> 00:11:37.954
One of the things that really
helped me in my early days

00:11:37.954 --> 00:11:40.646
as an entrepreneur, was reading this book,

00:11:40.646 --> 00:11:42.972
Radicals and Visionaries,
every single morning.

00:11:42.972 --> 00:11:44.693
And it was just three or four pages

00:11:44.693 --> 00:11:45.997
of a different entrepreneur

00:11:45.997 --> 00:11:49.518
that helped me get in the
zone of being inspired

00:11:49.518 --> 00:11:52.222
but also, give me some
tactics of what I could do.

00:11:52.222 --> 00:11:54.726
And so now, I don't read the book anymore,

00:11:54.726 --> 00:11:56.077
but I watch videos.

00:11:56.077 --> 00:11:59.394
And it gives me the
motivation and also the ideas

00:11:59.394 --> 00:12:00.264
of what I can do.

00:12:00.264 --> 00:12:03.040
And so you need to make sure
that you're spending time

00:12:03.040 --> 00:12:06.427
at least every week investing in yourself.

00:12:06.427 --> 00:12:07.777
Factor that in.

00:12:07.777 --> 00:12:09.830
Don't let it happen by accident

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.962
or randomly on the weekends somewhere.

00:12:11.962 --> 00:12:14.753
Book it into your calendar
every single week,

00:12:14.753 --> 00:12:15.857
for every single day,

00:12:15.857 --> 00:12:17.833
so you are constantly
learning and growing.

00:12:17.833 --> 00:12:20.697
So that's my view on the seven
ways to structure your day

00:12:20.697 --> 00:12:21.530
for success.

00:12:21.530 --> 00:12:23.861
I'm curious to figure out
what did you guys think?

00:12:23.861 --> 00:12:25.176
What did you guys like the most?

00:12:25.176 --> 00:12:26.091
What did you agree with?

00:12:26.091 --> 00:12:27.653
Or what did you not agree with?

00:12:27.653 --> 00:12:29.809
And would you add an eight,
nine, ten to the list?

00:12:29.809 --> 00:12:31.116
Something I missed out?

00:12:31.116 --> 00:12:31.949
Let me know.

00:12:31.949 --> 00:12:33.255
Leave it in the comments below.

00:12:33.255 --> 00:12:34.897
I'm going to join in the discussion.

00:12:34.897 --> 00:12:37.384
I also want to give a quick
shout out to Darja Bardo.

00:12:37.384 --> 00:12:39.567
Thank you so much for
picking up a copy of my book,

00:12:39.567 --> 00:12:40.400
Your One Word,

00:12:40.400 --> 00:12:43.002
It really, really, really,
really, means a lot to me.

00:12:43.002 --> 00:12:44.371
So thank you guys for watching.

00:12:44.371 --> 00:12:45.612
I believe in you.

00:12:45.612 --> 00:12:47.897
I hope you continue to
believe in yourself.

00:12:47.897 --> 00:12:50.070
And whatever your one word is.

00:12:50.070 --> 00:12:50.967
Much love.

00:12:50.967 --> 00:12:52.467
I'll see you soon.

